hat issue's reproducer evidence.\n\n**Is the fix verified?** No, and the purpose is not achieved. A QML binding tracks every property read during evaluation, including reads inside the functions it calls. Both height functions still loop on `displayModel.count` (:206, :228), so each append still re-runs the walk. The known-issue reproducer was re-captured on 2026-10-02 at 19:12 UTC (committed in a19f47d9) and still records known_issue_reproduced. shell/ and test/ have not changed since 1636fbf4, so Menu.qml and the reproducer are identical at this head. A separate qml6 behaviour diff (outside the package) measured 232 passes / 27,027 row visits at both base and head. The PR's test passes (56/56 JUnit passed), but it checks only source text and a JS simulation. Diff coverage: no changed decision lines.\n\n**Compatibility.** The package states `compatible`: all 4 sources checked, 0 findings, 213 inputs over 5 partitions, mcdc_diff 85/85 decisions. No partition measures height or open cost, so this says nothing about the PR's performance goal.\n\n**Questions for a human.** Should this merge as the fix for #10601 while the quadratic walk remains? Can any state change now leave a stale height, given that searchDivider is no longer a dependency?\n\n**Traceability.** rowListHeight / dmenuRowListHeight trace to SW-REQ-260922-B757 (function level). 30 more requirements are code_changed through file-level traces. The PR test is left unmapped on purpose. It asserts source text and a JS model, so it witnesses no requirement. The requirement it aims at, a bound on menu-open cost, does not exist yet and would not hold at this head (spec_gap). That is the `unmapped_code` disclosure (prevents ready) behind next decision more_evidence / missing_execution_evidence (1 gap). Readiness: not_assessed. effects_unavailable: no QML effect facts.\n\n**Not caused by this PR.** checks_skipped: 13 gates were skipped by configuration, as at the base. No gate failed."}
